hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27555","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib narrated to me, he said: Ali ibn Husayn sent me to al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra, and I asked her about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She brought out for him, meaning a vessel holding a mudd or about a mudd and a quarter. Sufyan said: As if he means the Hashimi. She said: I used to bring out water for him in this, and he would pour upon his hands three times - and at one time he said: he washes his hands before inserting them - and washes his face three times, rinses his mouth three times, sniffs water three times, washes his right hand three times and the left three times, wipes his head - and at one time he said: once or twice - front to back, then washes his feet three times. A cousin of yours came to me asking, and he is Ibn Abbas, and I informed him, and he said: I find in the Book of Allah only two wipings and two washings."
"27556","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, he said: al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra narrated to me, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to us often. He came to us and we placed the ablution vessel for him. He performed ablution: washed his palms three times, rinsed his mouth and sniffed water once each, washed his face three times, his forearms three times, wiped his head with what remained of his ablution water in his hands twice, beginning from its back then returning his hand to his forelock, washed his feet three times, and wiped his ears, front and back."
"27557","Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Dhakwan, from al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra, she said: We used to go out in campaigns with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, giving drink to the people, serving them, and returning the wounded and slain to Madinah."
"27558","Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us and we placed the ablution vessel for him. He performed ablution three times each, wiped his head twice, beginning from its back, and inserted his fingers into his ears."
"27559","Waki narrated to us, from Hasan, from Ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution and inserted his fingers into the cavities of his ears."
"27560","Waki narrated to us, from Sharik, from Ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh, she said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a basket containing fresh dates and small cucumbers, and he placed something in my hand and said: Adorn yourself with this and clothe yourself with this."
"27561","Abd al-Samad and Muhanna ibn Abd al-Hamid Abu Shibl narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Dhakwan, Abd al-Samad said in his hadith: Abu al-Husayn narrated to us, from al-Rubayyi, and Khalid said in his hadith: al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra narrated to me, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me on my wedding day and sat in the place of this bedding of mine, while with me were two slave girls beating the duff and eulogizing my forefathers killed on the day of Badr. They said in their saying: And among us is a Prophet who knows what will be today and tomorrow. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As for this, do not say it."
"27562","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution with her, and I saw him wipe over his head along the courses of hair, what comes forward and what goes back, and wipe his temples and ears, outer and inner."
"27563","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra, she said: I gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a basket of fresh dates and small cucumbers. She said: He gave me two handfuls of jewelry, or he said: gold, and said: Adorn yourself with this."
"27564","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution with her and wiped the whole head from above the hair, every side toward where the hair falls, without moving the hair from its form."
"27565","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, he said: Rubayyi bint Muawwidh narrated to me, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent among the villages of the Ansar: Whoever among you was fasting, let him complete his fast, and whoever ate, let him fast the rest of his day."
"27566","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Dhakwan informed us, he said: I asked al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra about the fast of Ashura. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of Ashura: Whoever among you woke fasting? He said: They said: Among us the fasting and among us the breaking. He said: Complete the rest of your day, and send to those around Madinah to complete the rest of their day."
"27567","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Husayn narrated to us, he said: There was a day for the people of Madinah when they played. I entered upon al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra, and she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me and sat in the place of this bedding of mine, while with me were two slave girls eulogizing my forefathers killed on the day of Badr, beating the duffs - and Affan at one time said: the duff - and they said in their saying: And among us is a Prophet who knows what will be tomorrow. He said: As for this, do not say it."
"27568","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution with her and wiped with his head the whole head from behind the hair, every side toward where the hair falls, without moving the hair from its form."
